.TH std::sub_match::sub_match 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::sub_match::sub_match \- std::sub_match::sub_match

.SH Synopsis
constexpr sub_match();  \fI(since C++11)\fP

Default constructs a std::sub_match. The matched member is set to false and the inherited
members first and second are value-initialized.

This is the only publicly accessible and defined constructor.

.SH Example


// Run this code

#include <cassert>
#include <regex>

int main()
{
    std::sub_match<const char*> s;
    assert(!s.matched);
}
